THOUGHT 1: The detection call failed due to an API/endpoint error. I'll handle this by (1) trying detection again with a simpler single label ("cup"), and (2) if that also fails, falling back to sliding_window_detection to search for the measuring cup/scale. I'll display whatever annotated outputs are returned so we can inspect and proceed.

ACTION 1:
```python
# ACTION 1: Robust detection with fallback to sliding window search
try:
    image_1_detection, image_1_boxes = detection(image_1, ["measuring cup", "cup", "graduation", "scale"])
    display(image_1_detection.annotated_image)
    print("Detected boxes (detection):", image_1_boxes)
except Exception as e:
    print("Initial detection failed with error:", repr(e))
    print("Attempting simpler detection with a single label 'cup'...")
    try:
        image_1_detection, image_1_boxes = detection(image_1, ["cup"])
        display(image_1_detection.annotated_image)
        print("Detected boxes (simple detection):", image_1_boxes)
    except Exception as e2:
        print("Simple detection also failed with error:", repr(e2))
        print("Falling back to sliding_window_detection to search for the cup/scale...")
        try:
            patches, patches_boxes = sliding_window_detection(image_1, ["cup", "measuring cup", "scale", "graduation"])
            if not patches:
                print("sliding_window_detection returned no patches.")
            else:
                for i, patch in enumerate(patches):
                    print(f"Patch {i}:")
                    display(patch.annotated_image)
                    # print boxes for this patch if available
                    if i < len(patches_boxes):
                        print("Boxes in this patch:", patches_boxes[i])
        except Exception as e3:
            print("sliding_window_detection also failed with error:", repr(e3))
            print("All detection attempts failed. Please try again later or provide a clearer image.")
